        "<b>Graded activity</b>: operant; baseline, then <b>time- or quota-contingent</b> progression regardless of pain; for deconditioning and pain-contingent behavior.",
        "<b>Graded exposure</b>: fear extinction; build a <b>fear hierarchy</b>, expose step by step to disconfirm harm; for high fear of specific movements.",
        "<b>EIH</b>: exercise usually reduces pain sensitivity; may be blunted in nociplastic pain, so start low, choose enjoyable exercise, progress gradually.",
        "<b>Pacing</b>: break up activity, baseline below flare threshold, gradual progression; breaks the boom-bust cycle.",
        "<b>Sleep</b>: bidirectional with pain; teach sleep hygiene; refer for suspected apnea or insomnia (CBT-I).",
        "<b>CBT-informed PT</b>: challenge unhelpful thoughts, graded goals, problem-solving, flare plans.",
